0	section	Approaching Nickolaus across the chasm
1	line	Nickolaus	Hello? Er... excuse me?
1	line	Nickolaus	Hello? Er... excuse me?
1	line	Player	Hello, are you Nickolaus?
1	line	Nickolaus	Aha, I see my reputation precedes me. Yes, I am the renowned hunter and explorer Nickolaus. You've arrived just in time to witness a very momentous occasion, for I have just discovered the nest of a giant
1	line	Nickolaus	eagle. And a most amazing discovery it is too, even if I do say so myself.
1	option	The Ardougne zookeeper sent me to find you.
2	line	Player	The Ardougne zookeeper sent me to find you.
2	line	Nickolaus	Ah yes, he sent me to find a ferret. A trivial task, and one which pales in comparison compared to this momentous discovery. I'm sure he can wait.
2	option	Well if you gave me a ferret I could take it back for you.
3	line	Player	Well if you gave me a ferret I could take it back for you.
3	line	Nickolaus	A ferret? I'm afraid I haven't had the chance to catch one yet, what with all this excitement.
3	action	above
2	option	So it's not that you're trapped then?
3	line	Player	So it's not that you're trapped then?
3	line	Nickolaus	Well I think trapped is quite a negative way of looking at it.
3	line	Nickolaus	I will admit however that getting out of here may be a little tricky. I did have a plan, but unfortunately it didn't involve being stuck in this nest.
3	option	Could I help at all?
4	line	Player	Could I help at all?
4	line	Nickolaus	Actually I believe you could. I need to somehow trick the eagles into thinking I'm one of them. Could you fashion some sort of disguise for me?
4	line	Player	What would that involve?
4	line	Nickolaus	Well, you could go and speak to the fancy dress shop owner in Varrock. He can make anything if you give him the right materials. In fact you should probably get a couple of disguises, one for each of us.
4	line	Player	That's a good idea. There are plenty of feathers around here. I'll see what I can do.
4	action	end
3	option	Well it'll give you a lot of time to study the eagles
4	line	Player	Well it'll give you a lot of time to study the eagles.
4	line	Nickolaus	Very true, and certainly an opportunity I wouldn't want to miss.
4	line	Player	Well, I'll let you get on with your work then.
4	line	Nickolaus	It's always a pleasure to discuss my discoveries.
4	action	end
1	option	Oh, but I'd come to rescue you.
2	line	Player	I've come to rescue you.
2	line	Nickolaus	How very kind of you. But Nickolaus Farrick never needs rescuing. I may apparently be trapped in a giant eagle's nest, but it is all a cunning ruse to put the beast at ease.
2	option	Aren't giant eagles mythical?
3	action	below
2	option	Oh, so you're not really trapped?
3	line	Player	Oh, so you're not really trapped?
3	line	Nickolaus	Well I think trapped is quite a negative way of looking at it.
3	action	above
1	option	Aren't giant eagles mythical?
2	line	Player	Aren't giant eagles mythical?
2	line	Nickolaus	Oh many people believe so, yes, but my relentless exploration has paid off once again, for I stand now in the nest of such a supposedly mythical creature.
2	line	Player	How did you manage to find the nest?
2	line	Nickolaus	Through unfaltering dedication, attention to detail, oh, and I suppose there's the minor point that I got carried here by an eagle.
2	line	Player	So in fact the eagle found you?
2	line	Nickolaus	So it might appear to an amateur yes, and, well, I may have been a little lucky, but it's still a remarkable discovery don't you think?
2	option	Amazing, but what do you intend to do now you've discovered it?
3	line	Player	Amazing, but what do you intend to do now you've discovered it?
3	line	Nickolaus	Well, there's all sorts to do. I need to observe its behaviour patterns and document its feeding habits. The discovery is only just the beginning you know.
3	option	I think you're trapped.
4	line	Player	I think you're trapped.
4	line	Nickolaus	Well I think trapped is quite a negative way of looking at it.
4	action	above
3	option	Well, I'll let you get on with your work then.
4	line	Player	Well, I'll let you get on with your work then.
4	line	Nickolaus	It's always a pleasure to discuss my discoveries.
4	action	end
2	option	Well, I'll let you get on with your work then.
3	line	Player	Well, I'll let you get on with your work then.
3	line	Nickolaus	It's always a pleasure to discuss my discoveries.
3	action	end
0	section	Shouting at Nickolaus
1	line	Player	Hello Nickolaus, how are you getting on with your discoveries?
1	line	Nickolaus	Wonderfully, these giant eagles are simply magnificent creatures. I absolutely must see about getting one as a pet.
1	option	The Ardougne zookeeper sent me to find you.
2	action	replay
1	option	A pet? Are you crazy?
2	line	Player	A pet? Are you crazy?
2	line	Nickolaus	Quite possibly, quite possibly, but I haven't found a creature I couldn't tame yet.
2	action	above
1	option	I've come to rescue you.
2	action	replay
1	option	Aren't giant eagles mythical?
2	action	replay
0	section	Visiting Nickolaus after agreeing to help him
1	line	Player	Hello Nickolaus, how are you getting on with your discoveries?
1	line	Nickolaus	Wonderfully thank you, although I am still having just a little trouble convincing them to let me leave.
1	line	Nickolaus	I don't suppose you've managed to get that disguise I asked for yet?
1	line	Player	I'm afraid not yet.
1	line	Nickolaus	Well like I said, the Varrock fancy dress shop is a good bet if you have the materials, and there are plenty of feathers around here.
1	line	Nickolaus	And while you're working on that, I'll get back to studying these incredible winged wonders.
1	action	end
0	section	Getting a bird costume
1	line	Asyff	Now you look like someone who goes to a lot of fancy dress parties.
1	line	Player	Errr...what are you saying exactly?
1	line	Asyff	I'm just saying that perhaps you would like to peruse my selection of garments.
1	line	Asyff	Or, if that doesn't interest you, then maybe you have something else to offer? I'm always on the look out for interesting or unusual new materials.
1	option	Okay, lets see what you've got then.
2	line	Player	Okay, lets see what you've got then.
2	line	Asyff	Have a look through my stock whenever you like; just ask to trade.
2	action	end
1	option	Well, specifically I'm after a couple of bird costumes.
2	line	Player	Well, specifically I'm after a couple of bird costumes.
2	line	Asyff	Ah, an inspired choice. What kind of bird were you thinking of?
2	line	Player	A giant eagle.
2	line	Asyff	Very interesting. Unfortunately I don't think I have any giant eagle costumes in stock at the moment.
2	line	Asyff	Of course if I had the materials I could make them for you.
2	line	Player	What materials would you need?
2	line	Asyff	Well, the main problem is that I'm fresh out of giant eagle feathers. I've been meaning to get onto my supplier about that for some time.
2	line	Player	Wait a second, you have a supplier? But I thought nobody knew where to find the nests?
2	line	Asyff	Well, there was some chap in desert clothing. He said his name was Ali. He assured me they were giant eagle feathers, although when I come to think about it they were suspiciously similar to chicken feathers.
2	line	Asyff	Anyway, you're probably looking at about 10 giant eagle feathers, assuming you can find a nest.
2	line	Asyff	I'd also need some swamp tar to hold things together and some yellow dye for the beaks. Everything else I can supply myself.
2	line	Player	I'll see what I can do.
2	action	end
1	option	I think I might just leave the perusing for now thanks.
2	line	Player	I think I might just leave the perusing for now thanks.
2	line	Asyff	Suit yourself. You know where I am if you change your mind.
2	action	end
1	option	Can you make clothing suitable for hunting in?
2	line	Player	Can you make clothing suitable for hunting in?
2	line	Asyff	Certainly, if you bring me the furs. Fur clothing is my speciality; ask me about it any time.
2	action	end
1	option	What sort of unusual materials did you have in mind?
2	line	Player	What sort of unusual materials did you have in mind?
2	line	Asyff	Oh, furs, feathers, anything a hunter might bring back from the wilds. I can make something out of almost anything.
2	action	end
